            <ArticleTitle>Acute myocardial infarction secondary to coronary vasospasm during withdrawal from industrial nitroglycerin exposure--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>143-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Industrial exposure to nitrates is known to produce acute and chronic effects on the cardiovascular system. A case of acute inferior myocardial infarction in a young, otherwise healthy, white male that occurred during the usual weekend withdrawal period is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
